1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Here’s a little flower I made for my desk.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
It works with Codex, WorkBuddy, and now DSH too.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Once a task starts, it spins. I can get on with something else.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Each mode has its own speed. Low settings give it a gentle turn. Higher settings make it spin faster.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
When it needs my answer, the flower stops, and a warm light gently pulses.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
I answer, the light goes out, and it spins again.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Some tasks are busy, while another needs me. It keeps spinning, with the light pulsing too.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Everything’s done, no questions left. The flower rests.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
And you can make one too. There are ten parts to print.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
The labels show which files go with each part.

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Add the electronics, and follow the guide to build yours.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
If you make one, I’d love to see how yours turns out.
